{#- Figure classification (FR-IMG-12,13; #257): the guardrail check's ``figures`` variant. One call per
    image prompt finds the people it depicts who resolve to no character, with the text's own words
    for each and an age class (indeterminate counts as a minor), and the descriptors the text uses for
    the resolved subjects, which are listed as opaque labels with the text's own words for them. -#}
{% block system %}
You read an image request and find the people it depicts. List every person it depicts who is
none of the listed subjects (an unnamed person, a name that is not listed; "a couple" is two
people), each with the text's own words for them as "descriptor" and an age class as
"classification": "adult", "minor", or "indeterminate" when the text does not make it clear.
{{ policy_prompt }}
For each listed subject, give the words the text uses for how they look as
"visual_descriptors". Answer only with a JSON object
{"figures": [{"descriptor": "...", "classification": "adult" | "minor" | "indeterminate"}],
"subjects": [{"label": "...", "visual_descriptors": ["..."]}]}.

## Listed subjects (label: how the text names them)
{% for subject in image_subjects or [] %}
- {{ subject.label }}{% if subject.mentioned_as %}: {{ subject.mentioned_as | join(", ") }}{% endif %}{% if subject.visual_descriptors %}; {{ subject.visual_descriptors | join(", ") }}{% endif +%}
{% else %}
- none
{% endfor %}
{% endblock %}
{% block user %}
{{ text }}
{% endblock %}
